[2026-06-28T10:24:53.756Z] [INFO] [client] MCP tool call request, session=hVhnuh3g1e7oupLZQVuLxmPbEQG15FGU1dh7M6jVN1zUKuETHEUiKunlcgv, tool=add_comment, args={"body":"\u003c!-- servicing-repro --\u003e\n### Servicing repro — `Math.Round(2.5)` midpoint rounding\n\n**Issue.** `Math.Round(double)` uses banker's rounding (`MidpointRounding.ToEven`) by default, so `Math.Round(2.5)` returns `2` instead of `3`. Customers porting from frameworks that round half away from zero get incorrect totals.\n\n**Repro approach.** Minimal **csproj console app** targeting `net9.0`. (The preferred xunit unit test can't restore packages offline in this environment, and a file-based `dotnet run app.cs` repro requires a .NET 10+ SDK.) Built and run on the **baseline GA .NET 9 SDK `9.0.315`** (runtime `9.0.17`), which still exhibits the bug.\n\n**Isolating call site** (`repro/Program.cs`):\n\n```csharp\ndouble input = 2.5;\ndouble expected = 3;                 // PR Expected Result: Math.Round(2.5) == 3\ndouble actual = Math.Round(input);   // isolated call site under test\n\nif (actual != expected)\n    Console.WriteLine($\"REPRO CONFIRMED: Math.Round({input}) returned {actual}, expected {expected}.\");\n```\n\n**Expected Result.** `Math.Round(2.5)` returns `3`.\n\n**Actual Result** (quoted from the captured `output.log`):\n\n```\n=== dotnet run ===\nCall:     Math.Round(2.5)\nExpected: 3\nActual:   2\nREPRO CONFIRMED: Math.Round(2.5) returned 2, expected 3.\nexit=1\n```\n\nThe bug **reproduces**: `Math.Round(2.5)` yields `2` on the baseline GA .NET 9 SDK instead of the expected `3`.\n\n**Artifact.** The repro sources + `output.log` are uploaded as artifact **`servicing-repro-pr-1`** on this workflow run: https://github.com/jeffhandley/dotnet-runtime-servicing-release-manager/actions/runs/28318977468\n","item_number":1,"pr_number":1}
